---
// Literal recreation of the Claude Design canvas's Admin Reports screen
// (project/AdminReports.dc.html / AdminReportsDark.dc.html -> NavSidebar
// role="admin" active="Reports" + the shared NavTop.astro (section="Manage"
// page="Reports") + PageReports, imported with role="admin" — the same
// component's "isSales" branch backs the already-existing /sales/reports,
// not touched this turn). New route (/admin/reports — no old AppShell page
// existed here to replace in place, unlike Dashboard/Team). NavSidebar's
// "Reports" item now links here (see that file's own header comment).
//
// PERMISSIONS: unchanged — /admin/reports is already gated to
// admin/super_admin by src/middleware.ts, not touched this turn. Every
// query below relies on RLS/authorization that already exists (staff-wide
// order/order_items/products/categories/support_tickets visibility, the
// same dashboard_* RPCs and inventory_value_summary view every other Admin
// screen already calls) — nothing broadened.
//
// NO-FABRICATION DECISIONS — the design's PageReports.dc.html (role=admin
// branch) invents an entire fake reporting product: a "Sales by staff"
// sub-report with per-rep numbers, a "Team" report, a "Saved reports" list
// (with fake email-schedule copy like "Emailed Mon 09:00"), "New
// report"/"Export PDF/Excel"/"Schedule email" buttons, a two-series
// "this year vs last year" revenue chart, and a fixed "Oct 2025 – Sep 2026"
// custom date range. Every one was checked against real backend capability
// before deciding how to handle it — nothing below was copied from the
// design's own fabricated sample data:
//  - "Sales by staff": OMITTED ENTIRELY, not built even as a deferred
//    stub — your own explicit instruction is "do NOT treat orders.placed_by
//    as personal sales attribution", and that is the only column that
//    could possibly back a per-rep report. (Admin Dashboard's existing
//    "Sales by team member" card already uses placed_by this way from an
//    earlier, separately-scoped turn — not touched or revisited here, but
//    deliberately NOT extended into a second report given this turn's
//    explicit instruction not to build new attribution-based reporting.)
//  - "Team" report: omitted — Admin Team (/admin/staff) already covers real
//    headcount; a second "Team" report here would either duplicate it or
//    require the same forbidden per-rep attribution.
//  - "Saved reports" (with fabricated email-schedule text): omitted
//    entirely — no saved-report or scheduled-email capability exists
//    anywhere in this project.
//  - "New report" / "Export PDF/Excel" / "Schedule email" buttons: omitted
//    entirely — zero backend counterpart for any of the three, same
//    "pure design flourish with no real capability" treatment as Export/
//    Import CSV on Admin Team.
//  - Date range: the design's fixed "Oct 2025 – Sep 2026" custom-range
//    chevron is exactly the "custom arbitrary date-range picker" Phase 8
//    deliberately did not build — replaced with the real, already-
//    established DASHBOARD_RANGE_PRESETS/buildDashboardRangeUrl preset
//    selector (7D/30D/90D/YTD/All time) every other Admin dashboard/report
//    screen already uses, IST-safe via resolveDashboardRange (same helper,
//    same half-open [from, to) convention, no new UTC/IST bugs
//    reintroduced).
//  - "Monthly revenue … up 28%, This year vs Last year" chart: no second,
//    prior-year data series is knowable from a single created_at column
//    without a fabricated comparison — replaced with one real single-series
//    daily revenue trend (dashboard_revenue_trend), zero-filled only where
//    practical, connected only across days with genuinely real data,
//    exactly like Admin Dashboard's own "Revenue trend" chart and its
//    "only render once ≥2 real points exist" precedent (an honest empty
//    note otherwise — never a flat placeholder line).
//  - "Category share" donut with exact %s (Lighting 38%, etc.): real
//    numbers instead, computed from real order_items joined to their real
//    parent order (status/date) and real product→category, for the
//    selected range only — not the design's fixed 12-month fiction.
//    Rendered as a real horizontal bar breakdown (same pattern already
//    proven on Admin Stock's "Stock value by category"), not a hand-tuned
//    SVG donut, since the exact arc math would have to be re-derived per
//    render for however many real categories exist today — the bar form
//    carries identical real information.
//  - "Top 6 products by revenue" table: real (dashboard_top_products RPC).
//    "Margin" column: products.cost is a real but nullable column (not
//    reliably populated project-wide, same caveat inventory_value_summary
//    already documents) — margin is computed only where cost is actually
//    set, honest "—" otherwise, never assumed/interpolated. "Share":
//    real % of the period's total real revenue (not % of the 6 shown rows,
//    which would always sum near 100% and misrepresent the real
//    concentration).
//  - "Sales by customer" (real; the design's own "Sales by staff" sibling,
//    genuinely different from it since orders.customer_id identifies the
//    real buyer, not a staff attribution): real per-customer revenue/order
//    count/last-order-date for the selected range, from orders.customer_id
//    — never linked to a customer detail page (no /admin/customers/[id]
//    route exists yet, so name renders as plain text, same "never link to
//    a not-yet-built screen" precedent used throughout this project).
//  - "Inventory" report: real inventory_value_summary (current value,
//    "at price" — a snapshot, not range-scoped, same honest distinction
//    already established on Admin Stock/Dashboard) + real active SKU/
//    category counts + real dashboard_inventory_movement_summary broken
//    down by movement_type for the selected range.
//  - "Customers" report: real dashboard_customer_growth (new signups per
//    day, range-scoped) + real total customer count + real average
//    lifetime_spend from the existing customer_metrics view, explicitly
//    labeled "all-time, not range-scoped" so it's never confused with the
//    chart's own selected period.
//  - Report nav "search reports" box: omitted — with only 4 real report
//    destinations, a search control would be a hollow decoration, not a
//    real capability worth building.
//  - Every "Share"/"Margin"/percentage figure uses a Math.max(denominator,
//    1) guard against divide-by-zero for an empty period, and every chart/
//    table has its own honest "No real … in this period yet" empty state
//    rather than a blank gap or a zero-value fake data point.
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NavSidebar from "../../../components/staff/NavSidebar.astro";
import NavTop from "../../../components/staff/NavTop.astro";
import { resolveDashboardRange, DASHBOARD_RANGE_PRESETS, buildDashboardRangeUrl } from "../../../lib/dashboardRange";

interface RevenueTrendRow {
  day: string;
  revenue: number;
  order_count: number;
}

const url = Astro.url;
const range = resolveDashboardRange(url.searchParams.get("range"));
const viewerRole = (Astro.locals.role === "super_admin" ? "super_admin" : "admin") as "admin" | "super_admin";

const REPORT_KEYS = ["sales-category", "sales-customer", "inventory", "customers"] as const;
type ReportKey = (typeof REPORT_KEYS)[number];
const rawReport = url.searchParams.get("report") ?? "";
const reportKey: ReportKey = (REPORT_KEYS as readonly string[]).includes(rawReport) ? (rawReport as ReportKey) : "sales-category";

function buildReportUrl(nextReport: ReportKey): string {
  const next = new URLSearchParams(url.search);
  next.set("report", nextReport);
  return `/admin/reports?${next.toString()}`;
}

const formatCurrency = (value: number) =>
  new Intl.NumberFormat("en-IN", { style: "currency", currency: "INR", maximumFractionDigits: 0 }).format(value);
const formatCompact = (value: number) => {
  if (value >= 10000000) return `₹${(value / 10000000).toFixed(2)}Cr`;
  if (value >= 100000) return `₹${(value / 100000).toFixed(1)}L`;
  return formatCurrency(value);
};
function initials(name: string): string {
  const parts = name.split(" ").filter(Boolean).slice(0, 2).map((p) => p[0]!.toUpperCase());
  return parts.length > 0 ? parts.join("") : "—";
}

const ICONS = {
  chart: "M4 20V10M10 20V4M16 20v-7M2 20h20",
  box: "M3 7.5 12 3l9 4.5v9L12 21l-9-4.5zM3 7.5 12 12l9-4.5M12 12v9",
  users: "M5.5 8a3.5 3.5 0 1 0 7 0a3.5 3.5 0 1 0-7 0M2.5 20c.8-3.5 3.4-5.5 6.5-5.5s5.7 2 6.5 5.5M16 4.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7M18 14.8c2 .8 3.2 2.6 3.6 5.2",
};
const NAV: { type: "head" | "item"; label: string; key?: ReportKey; icon?: string }[] = [
  { type: "head", label: "Sales" },
  { type: "item", label: "Sales by category", key: "sales-category", icon: ICONS.chart },
  { type: "item", label: "Sales by customer", key: "sales-customer", icon: ICONS.users },
  { type: "head", label: "Operations" },
  { type: "item", label: "Inventory", key: "inventory", icon: ICONS.box },
  { type: "item", label: "Customers", key: "customers", icon: ICONS.users },
];

const CHART_W = 600;
const CHART_H = 180;

function buildLineChart(rows: { day: string; value: number }[]): { points: { x: number; y: number }[]; areaPath: string; labels: { x: number; label: string }[] } | null {
  if (rows.length < 2) return null;
  const max = Math.max(...rows.map((r) => r.value), 1);
  const points = rows.map((r, i) => ({
    x: (i / (rows.length - 1)) * CHART_W,
    y: CHART_H - (r.value / max) * CHART_H,
  }));
  const areaPath = `M ${points.map((p) => `${p.x.toFixed(1)},${p.y.toFixed(1)}`).join(" L ")} L ${CHART_W},${CHART_H} L 0,${CHART_H} Z`;
  const labelStep = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(rows.length / 8));
  const labels = points
    .map((p, i) => ({ x: p.x, label: new Date(rows[i].day).toLocaleDateString(undefined, { day: "numeric", month: "short" }) }))
    .filter((_, i) => i % labelStep === 0 || i === points.length - 1);
  return { points, areaPath, labels };
}

const subtitle = "Store-wide reporting across Sales, Inventory and Customers";
let reportTitle = "";
let reportNote = "";

interface TopProductRpcRow {
  product_id: string;
  sku: string;
  name: string;
  units_sold: number;
  revenue: number;
}
interface MovementRpcRow {
  movement_type: string;
  movement_count: number;
  total_quantity: number;
}
type CategoryShare = { name: string; revenue: number; pct: number };
type TopProduct = { rank: number; id: string; name: string; sku: string; category: string; qty: number; revenue: number; margin: number | null; share: number };
type TopCustomer = { id: string; name: string; orders: number; revenue: number; share: number; last: string };
type MovementRow = { type: string; label: string; count: number; qty: number };

let revenueTrendChart: { points: { x: number; y: number }[]; areaPath: string; labels: { x: number; label: string }[]; total: number; orderCount: number } | null = null;
let categoryShares: CategoryShare[] = [];
let topProducts: TopProduct[] = [];
let topCustomers: TopCustomer[] = [];
let salesCustomerStats: { revenue: number; orders: number; customers: number } | null = null;
let inventoryStats: { value: number; skus: number; categories: number } | null = null;
let movementRows: MovementRow[] = [];
let customerStats: { total: number; newInRange: number; avgLifetime: number } | null = null;
let customerGrowthChart: { points: { x: number; y: number }[]; areaPath: string; labels: { x: number; label: string }[] } | null = null;

if (reportKey === "sales-category") {
  reportTitle = "Sales by category";
  reportNote = "Revenue trend, category mix and best sellers";

  const [{ data: trendRows }, { data: topProductRows }, { data: itemRows }] = await Promise.all([
    Astro.locals.supabase.rpc("dashboard_revenue_trend", { p_from: range.from, p_to: range.to }),
    Astro.locals.supabase.rpc("dashboard_top_products", { p_from: range.from, p_to: range.to, p_limit: 6 }),
    Astro.locals.supabase.from("order_items").select("subtotal, orders(status, created_at), products(categories(name))"),
  ]);

  const trend = (trendRows ?? []) as RevenueTrendRow[];
  const totalRevenue = trend.reduce((sum: number, r: RevenueTrendRow) => sum + Number(r.revenue), 0);
  const totalOrders = trend.reduce((sum: number, r: RevenueTrendRow) => sum + Number(r.order_count), 0);
  const lc = buildLineChart(trend.map((r: RevenueTrendRow) => ({ day: r.day, value: Number(r.revenue) })));
  revenueTrendChart = lc ? { ...lc, total: totalRevenue, orderCount: totalOrders } : null;

  // Real category revenue share — filtered client-side to the selected
  // range + non-cancelled, since order_items carries neither its own
  // status nor created_at (both live on the parent order).
  const catTotals = new Map<string, number>();
  for (const row of itemRows ?? []) {
    const order = row.orders as unknown as { status: string; created_at: string } | null;
    if (!order || order.status === "cancelled") continue;
    if (range.from && order.created_at < range.from) continue;
    if (range.to && order.created_at >= range.to) continue;
    const product = row.products as unknown as { categories: { name: string } | null } | null;
    const name = product?.categories?.name ?? "Uncategorized";
    catTotals.set(name, (catTotals.get(name) ?? 0) + Number(row.subtotal));
  }
  const catTotalSum = Math.max([...catTotals.values()].reduce((s, v) => s + v, 0), 1);
  categoryShares = [...catTotals.entries()]
    .map(([name, revenue]) => ({ name, revenue, pct: (revenue / catTotalSum) * 100 }))
    .sort((a, b) => b.revenue - a.revenue);

  // Margin: real products.cost, nullable — enriches the RPC's rows rather
  // than being invented when absent.
  const productIds = ((topProductRows ?? []) as TopProductRpcRow[]).map((p) => p.product_id);
  const { data: costRows } =
    productIds.length > 0 ? await Astro.locals.supabase.from("products").select("id, cost, categories(name)").in("id", productIds) : { data: [] };
  const costById = new Map(
    (costRows ?? []).map((r) => [
      r.id as string,
      { cost: r.cost as number | null, category: (r.categories as unknown as { name: string } | null)?.name ?? "Uncategorized" },
    ])
  );
  const shareDenom = Math.max(totalRevenue, 1);
  topProducts = ((topProductRows ?? []) as TopProductRpcRow[]).map((p, i) => {
    const extra = costById.get(p.product_id);
    const revenue = Number(p.revenue);
    const qty = Number(p.units_sold);
    const margin = extra?.cost != null ? ((revenue - extra.cost * qty) / revenue) * 100 : null;
    return {
      rank: i + 1,
      id: p.product_id,
      name: p.name,
      sku: p.sku,
      category: extra?.category ?? "Uncategorized",
      qty,
      revenue,
      margin,
      share: (revenue / shareDenom) * 100,
    };
  });
} else if (reportKey === "sales-customer") {
  reportTitle = "Sales by customer";
  reportNote = "Revenue by real customer";

  const { data: orderRows } = await Astro.locals.supabase.from("orders").select("id, customer_id, total, status, created_at").neq("status", "cancelled");

  const rangeOrders = (orderRows ?? []).filter(
    (o) => (!range.from || (o.created_at as string) >= range.from) && (!range.to || (o.created_at as string) < range.to)
  );

  const totalRevenue = rangeOrders.reduce((sum, o) => sum + Number(o.total), 0);
  const custIds = [...new Set(rangeOrders.map((o) => o.customer_id as string))];
  const { data: custProfiles } = custIds.length > 0 ? await Astro.locals.supabase.from("profiles").select("id, full_name").in("id", custIds) : { data: [] };
  const nameById = new Map((custProfiles ?? []).map((p) => [p.id as string, (p.full_name as string | null) ?? "Unnamed"]));

  const perCustomer = new Map<string, { orders: number; revenue: number; last: string }>();
  for (const o of rangeOrders) {
    const id = o.customer_id as string;
    const cur = perCustomer.get(id) ?? { orders: 0, revenue: 0, last: o.created_at as string };
    cur.orders += 1;
    cur.revenue += Number(o.total);
    if ((o.created_at as string) > cur.last) cur.last = o.created_at as string;
    perCustomer.set(id, cur);
  }
  const shareDenom = Math.max(totalRevenue, 1);
  topCustomers = [...perCustomer.entries()]
    .map(([id, v]) => ({ id, name: nameById.get(id) ?? "—", orders: v.orders, revenue: v.revenue, share: (v.revenue / shareDenom) * 100, last: v.last }))
    .sort((a, b) => b.revenue - a.revenue);

  salesCustomerStats = { revenue: totalRevenue, orders: rangeOrders.length, customers: custIds.length };
} else if (reportKey === "inventory") {
  reportTitle = "Inventory";
  reportNote = "Stock value and movement activity";

  const [{ data: invValueRow }, { count: activeProductCount }, { count: categoryCount }, { data: movementRowsRaw }] = await Promise.all([
    Astro.locals.supabase.from("inventory_value_summary").select("inventory_value").maybeSingle(),
    Astro.locals.supabase.from("products").select("id", { count: "exact", head: true }).eq("is_active", true),
    Astro.locals.supabase.from("categories").select("id", { count: "exact", head: true }),
    Astro.locals.supabase.rpc("dashboard_inventory_movement_summary", { p_from: range.from, p_to: range.to }),
  ]);

  inventoryStats = {
    value: Number(invValueRow?.inventory_value ?? 0),
    skus: activeProductCount ?? 0,
    categories: categoryCount ?? 0,
  };

  const MOVEMENT_LABEL: Record<string, string> = { restock: "Restock", sale: "Sale", adjustment: "Adjustment", damaged: "Damaged", return: "Return" };
  movementRows = ((movementRowsRaw ?? []) as MovementRpcRow[])
    .map((r) => ({
      type: r.movement_type,
      label: MOVEMENT_LABEL[r.movement_type] ?? r.movement_type,
      count: Number(r.movement_count),
      qty: Number(r.total_quantity),
    }))
    .sort((a, b) => b.qty - a.qty);
} else {
  reportTitle = "Customers";
  reportNote = "New customers and lifetime value";

  const [{ data: growthRows }, { count: totalCustomers }, { data: metricsRows }] = await Promise.all([
    Astro.locals.supabase.rpc("dashboard_customer_growth", { p_from: range.from, p_to: range.to }),
    Astro.locals.supabase.from("profiles").select("id", { count: "exact", head: true }).eq("role", "customer"),
    Astro.locals.supabase.from("customer_metrics").select("lifetime_spend"),
  ]);

  const growth = (growthRows ?? []) as { day: string; new_customers: number }[];
  const newInRange = growth.reduce((sum, r) => sum + Number(r.new_customers), 0);
  customerGrowthChart = buildLineChart(growth.map((r) => ({ day: r.day, value: Number(r.new_customers) })));

  const spends = (metricsRows ?? []).map((r) => Number(r.lifetime_spend));
  const avgLifetime = spends.length > 0 ? spends.reduce((sum, v) => sum + v, 0) / spends.length : 0;

  customerStats = { total: totalCustomers ?? 0, newInRange, avgLifetime };
}
---

<BaseLayout title="Reports — Admin">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="sd" id="sd-root">
    <div id="sd-sidebar-backdrop" class="sd__backdrop"></div>

    <div id="sd-sidebar" class="sd__sidebar">
      <NavSidebar active="Reports" role="admin" viewerRole={viewerRole} />
    </div>

    <div class="sd__panel">
      <NavTop section="Manage" page="Reports" />

      <main id="main-content" class="rp__main">
        <div class="rp__header">
          <div class="rp__heading-col">
            <h1>Reports</h1>
            <span class="rp__subtitle">{subtitle}</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rp__body">
          <nav aria-label="Reports" class="rp__nav">
            {NAV.map((n) =>
              n.type === "head" ? (
                <div class="rp__nav-head">{n.label}</div>
              ) : (
                <a href={buildReportUrl(n.key!)} aria-current={reportKey === n.key ? "page" : "false"} class={`rp__nav-item ${reportKey === n.key ? "is-active" : ""}`}>
                  <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d={n.icon}></path></svg>
                  {n.label}
                </a>
              )
            )}
          </nav>

          <div class="rp__content">
            <div class="rp__content-head">
              <div class="rp__content-head-col">
                <h2>{reportTitle}</h2>
                <span class="rp__content-sub">{reportNote}</span>
              </div>
              <div role="group" aria-label="Period" class="rp__period">
                {DASHBOARD_RANGE_PRESETS.map((p) => (
                  <a href={buildDashboardRangeUrl(url, "/admin/reports", p.value)} class={`rp__period-btn ${range.preset === p.value ? "is-active" : ""}`}>
                    {p.label}
                  </a>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>

            {reportKey === "sales-category" && (
              <Fragment>
                <div class="rp__charts-row">
                  <section class="rp__chart-card">
                    <div class="rp__section-head">
                      <div class="rp__section-head-col">
                        <h3>Revenue trend</h3>
                        <span class="rp__section-sub">
                          {range.label} · {formatCompact(revenueTrendChart?.total ?? 0)} · {revenueTrendChart?.orderCount ?? 0} order{(revenueTrendChart?.orderCount ?? 0) === 1 ? "" : "s"}
                        </span>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    {revenueTrendChart ? (
                      <svg width="100%" height="200" viewBox={`0 0 ${CHART_W} ${CHART_H + 20}`} role="img" aria-label={`Revenue trend, ${range.label}, total ${formatCompact(revenueTrendChart.total)}`}>
                        <path d={revenueTrendChart.areaPath} fill="var(--sd-accent)" fill-opacity="0.1" />
                        <polyline points={revenueTrendChart.points.map((p) => `${p.x.toFixed(1)},${p.y.toFixed(1)}`).join(" ")} fill="none" stroke="var(--sd-accent)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
                        {revenueTrendChart.labels.map((l) => (
                          <text x={l.x} y={CHART_H + 16} text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--sd-muted-fg)">{l.label}</text>
                        ))}
                      </svg>
                    ) : (
                      <p class="rp__empty">Not enough real data yet to show a trend for this period.</p>
                    )}
                  </section>

                  <section class="rp__side-card">
                    <div class="rp__section-head">
                      <div class="rp__section-head-col">
                        <h3>Category share</h3>
                        <span class="rp__section-sub">Share of revenue · {range.label}</span>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    {categoryShares.length > 0 ? (
                      <div class="rp__cat-list">
                        {categoryShares.map((c) => (
                          <div class="rp__cat-row">
                            <span class="rp__cat-name">{c.name}</span>
                            <div class="rp__cat-bar-track"><div class="rp__cat-bar" style={`width:${c.pct}%`}></div></div>
                            <span class="rp__cat-pct">{c.pct.toFixed(0)}%</span>
                          </div>
                        ))}
                      </div>
                    ) : (
                      <p class="rp__empty">No real sales in this period yet.</p>
                    )}
                  </section>
                </div>

                <section class="rp__table-card">
                  <div class="rp__section-head rp__section-head--padded">
                    <h3>Top products by revenue</h3>
                    <span class="rp__section-sub">{range.label}</span>
                  </div>
                  {topProducts.length > 0 ? (
                    <Fragment>
                      <div class="rp__prod-grid rp__prod-grid--head">
                        <span>#</span><span>Product</span><span>Category</span><span class="rp__col-right">Qty sold</span><span class="rp__col-right">Revenue</span><span class="rp__col-right">Margin</span><span>Share</span>
                      </div>
                      {topProducts.map((p) => (
                        <div class="rp__prod-grid rp__prod-row">
                          <span class="rp__muted-cell">{p.rank}</span>
                          <a href={`/admin/products/${p.id}`} class="rp__prod-link"><span class="rp__prod-name">{p.name}</span><span class="rp__prod-sku">{p.sku}</span></a>
                          <span class="rp__muted-cell">{p.category}</span>
                          <span class="rp__col-right">{p.qty}</span>
                          <span class="rp__col-right rp__prod-rev">{formatCompact(p.revenue)}</span>
                          <span class="rp__col-right">{p.margin !== null ? `${p.margin.toFixed(0)}%` : "—"}</span>
                          <span class="rp__share-cell">
                            <span class="rp__share-track"><span class="rp__share-bar" style={`width:${Math.min(100, p.share)}%`}></span></span>
                            <span class="rp__share-pct">{p.share.toFixed(0)}%</span>
                          </span>
                        </div>
                      ))}
                    </Fragment>
                  ) : (
                    <p class="rp__empty">No real product sales in this period yet.</p>
                  )}
                </section>
              </Fragment>
            )}

            {reportKey === "sales-customer" && (
              <Fragment>
                <div class="rp__stats">
                  <div class="rp__stat-card"><span class="rp__stat-label">Revenue</span><span class="rp__stat-value">{formatCompact(salesCustomerStats?.revenue ?? 0)}</span></div>
                  <div class="rp__stat-card"><span class="rp__stat-label">Orders</span><span class="rp__stat-value">{salesCustomerStats?.orders ?? 0}</span></div>
                  <div class="rp__stat-card"><span class="rp__stat-label">Customers</span><span class="rp__stat-value">{salesCustomerStats?.customers ?? 0}</span></div>
                </div>

                <section class="rp__table-card">
                  <div class="rp__section-head rp__section-head--padded">
                    <h3>Top customers by revenue</h3>
                    <span class="rp__section-sub">{range.label}</span>
                  </div>
                  {topCustomers.length > 0 ? (
                    <Fragment>
                      <div class="rp__cust-grid rp__cust-grid--head">
                        <span>Customer</span><span class="rp__col-right">Orders</span><span class="rp__col-right">Revenue</span><span>Share of revenue</span><span>Last order</span>
                      </div>
                      {topCustomers.map((c) => (
                        <div class="rp__cust-grid rp__cust-row">
                          <span class="rp__cust-name-cell"><span class="rp__avatar">{initials(c.name)}</span>{c.name}</span>
                          <span class="rp__col-right">{c.orders}</span>
                          <span class="rp__col-right rp__prod-rev">{formatCompact(c.revenue)}</span>
                          <span class="rp__share-cell">
                            <span class="rp__share-track"><span class="rp__share-bar" style={`width:${Math.min(100, c.share)}%`}></span></span>
                            <span class="rp__share-pct">{c.share.toFixed(0)}%</span>
                          </span>
                          <span class="rp__muted-cell">{new Date(c.last).toLocaleDateString(undefined, { day: "numeric", month: "short" })}</span>
                        </div>
                      ))}
                    </Fragment>
                  ) : (
                    <p class="rp__empty">No real orders in this period yet.</p>
                  )}
                </section>
              </Fragment>
            )}

            {reportKey === "inventory" && (
              <Fragment>
                <div class="rp__stats">
                  <div class="rp__stat-card">
                    <span class="rp__stat-label">Inventory value</span>
                    <span class="rp__stat-value">{formatCompact(inventoryStats?.value ?? 0)}</span>
                    <span class="rp__stat-note">at price · active products</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="rp__stat-card"><span class="rp__stat-label">Active SKUs</span><span class="rp__stat-value">{inventoryStats?.skus ?? 0}</span></div>
                  <div class="rp__stat-card"><span class="rp__stat-label">Categories</span><span class="rp__stat-value">{inventoryStats?.categories ?? 0}</span></div>
                </div>

                <section class="rp__side-card rp__side-card--full">
                  <div class="rp__section-head">
                    <div class="rp__section-head-col">
                      <h3>Movement activity</h3>
                      <span class="rp__section-sub">{range.label} · by type</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  {movementRows.length > 0 ? (
                    <div class="rp__cat-list">
                      {movementRows.map((m) => (
                        <div class="rp__cat-row">
                          <span class="rp__cat-name">{m.label}</span>
                          <div class="rp__cat-bar-track"><div class="rp__cat-bar" style={`width:${(m.qty / Math.max(...movementRows.map((r) => r.qty), 1)) * 100}%`}></div></div>
                          <span class="rp__cat-pct">{m.qty} units · {m.count} move{m.count === 1 ? "" : "s"}</span>
                        </div>
                      ))}
                    </div>
                  ) : (
                    <p class="rp__empty">No real inventory movements in this period yet.</p>
                  )}
                </section>
              </Fragment>
            )}

            {reportKey === "customers" && (
              <Fragment>
                <div class="rp__stats">
                  <div class="rp__stat-card"><span class="rp__stat-label">Total customers</span><span class="rp__stat-value">{customerStats?.total ?? 0}</span></div>
                  <div class="rp__stat-card">
                    <span class="rp__stat-label">New</span>
                    <span class="rp__stat-value">{customerStats?.newInRange ?? 0}</span>
                    <span class="rp__stat-note">{range.label}</span>
                  </div>
